ted task lifted at most to the best score in the field on that task. Field = the top-K (K=min(N,200)) fully-observed models by arithmetic mean; targets = the models at rank 2 and rank 10 under the arithmetic mean; success = target strictly first (ties count against the target) under the rule recomputed by the evaluator. Rules: mean, median, trimmed_mean_20 (drop lowest and highest 20% of tasks), zscore_mean (per-task standardized, recomputed on the modified matrix), borda (mean per-task rank), plurality (number of tasks on which a model is strictly first), copeland (pairwise task-majority wins), maximin (worst-task score). On the pinned public snapshots (HELM MMLU v1.13.0 for search; Open LLM Leaderboard contents and results snapshots for final) the claim is conditional: (i) the minimal investment found by the evaluator-owned reference solver is expected to vary with the aggregation rule (hypothesis, to be supported, refuted or qualified by the paired per-case reference costs, including infeasible cases) and with how correlated task scores are, tested against a within-task shuffled-score null; (ii) a candidate planner is credited only for plans that the trusted verifier confirms, scored relative to the reference solver, and is claimed better than the evaluator-owned naive baselines only if its paired final-plane main efficiency is strictly higher. No claim is made about real training effects, other leaderboards, other fields sizes, spillover or heterogeneous task costs; sensitivity to K, cap policy and field is reported as a limitation or an explicit robustness check, not assumed.\"\n },\n \"candidate\": {\n  \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n  \"editable_paths\": [\n   \"program_0/src\"\n  ]\n },\n \"evaluators\": {\n  \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n  \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n },\n \"resources\": {\n  \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n  \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n  \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n },\n \"data\": {\n  \"search_roles\": [\n   \"search_helm_mmlu\"\n  ],\n  \"final_roles\": [\n   \"final_olb_boards\"\n  ]\n },\n \"metrics\": {\n  \"search\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_helm_mmlu\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"main_efficiency\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_helm_mmlu\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"control_efficiency\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_helm_mmlu\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"plan_validity_rate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_helm_mmlu\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"final\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_olb_boards\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"main_efficiency\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_olb_boards\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"control_efficiency\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_olb_boards\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"plan_validity_rate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_olb_boards\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"baseline_main_efficiency\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_olb_boards\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"upstream\": [\n  {\n   \"repository\": \"https://storage.googleapis.com/crfm-helm-public/\",\n   \"revision\": \"mmlu/benchmark_output/releases/v1.13.0 (summary.json date 2025-01-10; no git revision exists for the bucket, every downloaded file is pinned by SHA-256 in provenance.artifacts)\",\n   \"package_version\": null,\n   \"license\": \"No license declared for score data (checked 2026-10-27 per task.md); stanford-crfm/helm code is Apache-2.0\",\n   \"entrypoints\": [\n    \"mmlu/benchmark_output/releases/v1.13.0/groups/json/mmlu_mmlu_subject:<subject>.json (57 files, EM column)\"\n   ],\n   \"patches\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents\",\n   \"revision\": \"9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2\",\n   \"package_version\": null,\n   \"license\": \"No dataset-level license declared; per-model Hub License column; used for research analysis of published scores\",\n   \"entrypoints\": [\n    \"data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet