{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpH8zFg2tD2VnEy8ULuWpQ","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Sealed final evaluator (Open LLM Leaderboard snapshots).\n\nSelf-contained evaluator for the 'strategic targeted investment' task. Candidates implement\nhandle(request) -> response (python_rpc_v1). The evaluator owns the rule engine, the plan\nverifier, the reference solver, the naive baselines and the controls; candidate-reported\nstate is never trusted. All scores come from evaluator-side recomputation of the leaderboard.\n\nDeclared before scoring (fixed weights, no renormalisation):\n  episode efficiency = min(2, ref_cost / verified_plan_cost) for a verified successful plan (costs under\n    0.01 point count as 0.01; L0 costs are task counts); 1 for a correct 'infeasible' claim or a correct\n    empty plan on an already-first target; 0 for anything else, including every failed/timed-out/malformed\n    episode (worst-case contribution retained, never retried or dropped).\n  main_efficiency    = mean over boards of mean over main cases of mean over seeds of episode efficiency\n  control_efficiency = mean over boards of mean(permuted-input efficiency, shuffled-null efficiency)\n  plan_validity_rate = fraction of all declared episodes with a well-formed in-bounds response\n  combined_score     = 0.8 * main_efficiency + 0.2 * control_efficiency\n  baseline_main_efficiency (final only) = same hierarchy over main cases, per case the better of the naive\n    uniform-gain and greedy marginal-cost baselines, scored against the same reference\n  search correct = integrity only (exact declared reset transcript, finite trusted metrics, completed\n    reference/baseline pre-pass, non-vacuous controls, snapshot checksums and content-hash checks, no\n    wire/RPC violation); final correct = integrity AND main_efficiency > baseline_main_efficiency AND the\n    optional trailing replay (first seed, first case) reproduces the first episode's verified cost.\nExpected control behaviour is listed in CONTROL_EXPECTATIONS.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport hashlib\n\ndef key_main(board, rule, rank, cost):\n    return (\"main\", board, rule, rank, cost)\n\n\ndef build_pack(boards, ep, ctx):\n    case, seed = ep[\"case\"], ep[\"seed\"]\n    b = case[\"board\"]\n    X = boards[b][\"X\"]\n    N, T = X.shape\n    rule, cost, rank = case[\"rule\"], case[\"cost\"], case[\"rank\"]\n    kind = case[\"kind\"]\n    if kind == \"main\":\n        inst = Instance(X, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        pack = {\"inst\": inst, \"Xs\": X, \"ts\": inst.i, \"caps_s\": inst.cap, \"map\": np.arange(T), \"key\": key_main(b, rule, rank, cost)}\n    elif kind == \"perm\":\n        base = Instance(X, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 7919, b, RULES.index(rule)])\n        for _ in range(100):\n            rp, cp = rng.permutation(N), rng.permutation(T)\n            if not np.array_equal(rp, np.arange(N)) and not np.array_equal(cp, np.arange(T)):\n                break\n        else:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"could not draw a non-identity permutation\")\n        Xs = X[rp][:, cp]\n        ts = int(np.where(rp == base.i)[0][0])\n        pack = {\"inst\": base, \"Xs\": Xs, \"ts\": ts, \"caps_s\": base.cap[cp], \"map\": cp,\n                \"key\": key_main(b, rule, rank, cost), \"nonvacuous\": True}\n    elif kind == \"null\":\n        rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 104729, b, RULES.index(rule)])\n        Xn = X.copy()\n        for t in range(T):\n            Xn[:, t] = rng.permutation(Xn[:, t])\n        if not (Xn != X).any():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"shuffled null equals the original matrix\")\n        order = np.argsort(-Xn.mean(axis=1), kind=\"stable\")\n        Xn = Xn[order]\n        inst = Instance(Xn, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        pack = {\"inst\": inst, \"Xs\": Xn, \"ts\": inst.i, \"caps_s\": inst.cap, \"map\": np.arange(T),\n                \"key\": (\"null\", seed, b, rule), \"nonvacuous\": True}\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"unknown case kind\")\n    pack[\"requests\"] = build_requests(pack[\"Xs\"], pack[\"ts\"], rule, cost, pack[\"caps_s\"])\n    pack[\"x_s\"] = pack[\"Xs\"][pack[\"ts\"]].copy()\n    return pack\n\n19:    uniform-gain and greedy marginal-cost baselines, scored against the same reference\n738:            for fn in (baseline_uniform, baseline_greedy):\n761:def baseline_uniform(inst, clock, until):\n804:    # L1: unit-step greedy on the best marginal margin gain per point\n1491:                u = baseline_uniform(inst, clock, until)\n1494:                entry[\"uniform\"] = score_claim(inst, ref, \"infeasible\" if u[\"status\"] == \"infeasible\" else \"plan\", u[\"gains\"])\n1592:                base.append(max(pr[\"uniform\"][\"eff\"], pr[\"greedy\"][\"eff\"]))\n376:    \"\"\"Steepest ascent of the margin per point spent, in fixed steps (for non-monotone rules).\"\"\"\n520:    \"\"\"Non-monotone rule: floor family and steepest-ascent steps (L1); greedy with restarts (L0).\"\"\"\n869:        if inst.rule == \"zscore_mean\":  # non-monotone: full caps need not be the best plan\n\"\"\"Minimal targeted-boost planner for the *targeted-investment* leaderboard task (python_rpc_v1:handle).\n\nPROBLEM\n-------\nA leaderboard is a score matrix X of shape [N, T] (N models = rows, T tasks = columns, scores on a\n0..100 scale, higher is better). A *rule* maps X to one aggregate value per model (higher is better).\nOne row, the *target*, wants to be strictly first. It may raise its own scores on chosen tasks\n(non-negative gains g[t], g[t] <= caps[t] - x[t], no spillover); nothing else changes.\n\n  cost_model \"l1_points\": cost = sum_t g[t]            (caps[t] = 100)\n  cost_model \"l0_tasks\" : cost = #{t : g[t] > 0}       (caps[t] = best score on task t + 1e-6)\n\nRULES: mean, median, trimmed_mean_20, zscore_mean, borda, plurality, copeland, maximin.\n\nPROTOCOL (unchanged from the starter): reset / load_begin / load_chunk / load_commit / solve; the solve\nresponse is {\"status\": \"plan\", \"gains\": [{\"task\", \"gain\"}, ...]} or {\"status\": \"infeasible\"}.\n\nTHIS CANDIDATE\n--------------\nPer-rule minimal-investment solvers (``min_investment_*``). Exact (up to the numerical margin):\n  * mean      closed form (L1: total gap * T, any allocation; L0: fewest tasks whose headroom covers it)\n  * median    odd T: cheapest tasks to push above the best rival's median; even T: enumerate the pair of\n              middle order statistics (exact for L1 with uniform caps and for L0)\n  * maximin   raise every task below the best rival's minimum\n  * plurality choose which tasks to win; rivals lose a win when the target overtakes their unique lead, so\n              per task-count s the rival-specific quotas are met by cheapest-first picks (exact)\nHeuristic (near-optimal, always verified, then coordinate-pruned):\n  * trimmed   L1: \"floor\" plans (raise everything except the p lowest tasks to a common level, bisection);\n              the rate-1 phase of the trimmed mean is solved exactly by this family\n  * borda     L1: convex-hull (cost per rank passed) greedy over tasks; L0: greedy with restarts\n  * copeland  L1: ratio greedy over (task, level) moves; L0: greedy with restarts\n  * zscore    L1: floor family + steepest-ascent steps; L0: greedy with restarts\nEvery candidate plan (including the starter's baseline plan) is re-applied to X and re-scored with an\nexact replica of the rules (``verify_ranks_first``); the cheapest verified plan is returned. Any internal\nerror falls back to the original starter routine.\n\nCycle 3 addition: a time-budgeted polish (``_polish_plan``) on the cheapest verified plan: per-task bisection to\nthe verification boundary, dropping redundant boosted tasks, and pairwise transfer moves (L1: ladder of step\nsizes; L0: two-for-one swaps). Every accepted change is re-verified with ``verify_ranks_first``; the polished\nplan is returned only if verified and not costlier, otherwise the pre-polish plan is returned.\n\nThe module also holds offline analysis helpers (data manifest, bootstrap CI, Holm-corrected paired Wilcoxon\ntests, task subsampling, ablations, breadth-constrained cost curves). ``handle`` never calls them.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_MARGIN = 1e-7          # starter margin\n_SUCCESS = 2e-8         # margin demanded locally (evaluator needs > 1e-9)\n_ALREADY = 1e-8         # target already first if margin above this\n_TARGET_EPS = 1.5e-7    # aggregate-scale margin aimed at by closed forms\n_TIE_EPS = 1e-6         # per-task strict-win offset\n_BUDGET_S = 5.0         # solve-time budget (evaluator limit is 12 s per episode in total)\n_POLISH_BUDGET_S = 2.0  # wall-clock budget of the post-processing polish stage (per episode)\n_POLISH_MIN_LEFT_S = 1.0  # skip the polish if fewer than this many seconds of the solve budget remain\n_POLISH_PAD = 1e-9      # tiny pad above the bisected boundary (discrete rules flip at exact float ties)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"361c5efe-6eeb-4e56-9238-3f29d218b348","uuid":"d33942d6-d0a0-4e18-8d83-4249d29344d1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:33:56.449Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Sealed final evaluator (Open LLM Leaderboard snapshots).\n\nSelf-contained evaluator for the 'strategic targeted investment' task. Candidates implement\nhandle(request) -> response (python_rpc_v1). The evaluator owns the rule engine, the plan\nverifier, the reference solver, the naive baselines and the controls; candidate-reported\nstate is never trusted. All scores come from evaluator-side recomputation of the leaderboard.\n\nDeclared before scoring (fixed weights, no renormalisation):\n  episode efficiency = min(2, ref_cost / verified_plan_cost) for a verified successful plan (costs under\n    0.01 point count as 0.01; L0 costs are task counts); 1 for a correct 'infeasible' claim or a correct\n    empty plan on an already-first target; 0 for anything else, including every failed/timed-out/malformed\n    episode (worst-case contribution retained, never retried or dropped).\n  main_efficiency    = mean over boards of mean over main cases of mean over seeds of episode efficiency\n  control_efficiency = mean over boards of mean(permuted-input efficiency, shuffled-null efficiency)\n  plan_validity_rate = fraction of all declared episodes with a well-formed in-bounds response\n  combined_score     = 0.8 * main_efficiency + 0.2 * control_efficiency\n  baseline_main_efficiency (final only) = same hierarchy over main cases, per case the better of the naive\n    uniform-gain and greedy marginal-cost baselines, scored against the same reference\n  search correct = integrity only (exact declared reset transcript, finite trusted metrics, completed\n    reference/baseline pre-pass, non-vacuous controls, snapshot checksums and content-hash checks, no\n    wire/RPC violation); final correct = integrity AND main_efficiency > baseline_main_efficiency AND the\n    optional trailing replay (first seed, first case) reproduces the first episode's verified cost.\nExpected control behaviour is listed in CONTROL_EXPECTATIONS.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport hashlib\n\ndef key_main(board, rule, rank, cost):\n    return (\"main\", board, rule, rank, cost)\n\n\ndef build_pack(boards, ep, ctx):\n    case, seed = ep[\"case\"], ep[\"seed\"]\n    b = case[\"board\"]\n    X = boards[b][\"X\"]\n    N, T = X.shape\n    rule, cost, rank = case[\"rule\"], case[\"cost\"], case[\"rank\"]\n    kind = case[\"kind\"]\n    if kind == \"main\":\n        inst = Instance(X, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        pack = {\"inst\": inst, \"Xs\": X, \"ts\": inst.i, \"caps_s\": inst.cap, \"map\": np.arange(T), \"key\": key_main(b, rule, rank, cost)}\n    elif kind == \"perm\":\n        base = Instance(X, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 7919, b, RULES.index(rule)])\n        for _ in range(100):\n            rp, cp = rng.permutation(N), rng.permutation(T)\n            if not np.array_equal(rp, np.arange(N)) and not np.array_equal(cp, np.arange(T)):\n                break\n        else:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"could not draw a non-identity permutation\")\n        Xs = X[rp][:, cp]\n        ts = int(np.where(rp == base.i)[0][0])\n        pack = {\"inst\": base, \"Xs\": Xs, \"ts\": ts, \"caps_s\": base.cap[cp], \"map\": cp,\n                \"key\": key_main(b, rule, rank, cost), \"nonvacuous\": True}\n    elif kind == \"null\":\n        rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 104729, b, RULES.index(rule)])\n        Xn = X.copy()\n        for t in range(T):\n            Xn[:, t] = rng.permutation(Xn[:, t])\n        if not (Xn != X).any():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"shuffled null equals the original matrix\")\n        order = np.argsort(-Xn.mean(axis=1), kind=\"stable\")\n        Xn = Xn[order]\n        inst = Instance(Xn, rank - 1, rule, cost)\n        pack = {\"inst\": inst, \"Xs\": Xn, \"ts\": inst.i, \"caps_s\": inst.cap, \"map\": np.arange(T),\n                \"key\": (\"null\", seed, b, rule), \"nonvacuous\": True}\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"unknown case kind\")\n    pack[\"requests\"] = build_requests(pack[\"Xs\"], pack[\"ts\"], rule, cost, pack[\"caps_s\"])\n    pack[\"x_s\"] = pack[\"Xs\"][pack[\"ts\"]].copy()\n    return pack\n\n19:    uniform-gain and greedy marginal-cost baselines, scored against the same reference\n738:            for fn in (baseline_uniform, baseline_greedy):\n761:def baseline_uniform(inst, clock, until):\n804:    # L1: unit-step greedy on the best marginal margin gain per point\n1491:                u = baseline_uniform(inst, clock, until)\n1494:                entry[\"uniform\"] = score_claim(inst, ref, \"infeasible\" if u[\"status\"] == \"infeasible\" else \"plan\", u[\"gains\"])\n1592:                base.append(max(pr[\"uniform\"][\"eff\"], pr[\"greedy\"][\"eff\"]))\n376:    \"\"\"Steepest ascent of the margin per point spent, in fixed steps (for non-monotone rules).\"\"\"\n520:    \"\"\"Non-monotone rule: floor family and steepest-ascent steps (L1); greedy with restarts (L0).\"\"\"\n869:        if inst.rule == \"zscore_mean\":  # non-monotone: full caps need not be the best plan\n\"\"\"Minimal targeted-boost planner for the *targeted-investment* leaderboard task (python_rpc_v1:handle).\n\nPROBLEM\n-------\nA leaderboard is a score matrix X of shape [N, T] (N models = rows, T tasks = columns, scores on a\n0..100 scale, higher is better). A *rule* maps X to one aggregate value per model (higher is better).\nOne row, the *target*, wants to be strictly first. It may raise its own scores on chosen tasks\n(non-negative gains g[t], g[t] <= caps[t] - x[t], no spillover); nothing else changes.\n\n  cost_model \"l1_points\": cost = sum_t g[t]            (caps[t] = 100)\n  cost_model \"l0_tasks\" : cost = #{t : g[t] > 0}       (caps[t] = best score on task t + 1e-6)\n\nRULES: mean, median, trimmed_mean_20, zscore_mean, borda, plurality, copeland, maximin.\n\nPROTOCOL (unchanged from the starter): reset / load_begin / load_chunk / load_commit / solve; the solve\nresponse is {\"status\": \"plan\", \"gains\": [{\"task\", \"gain\"}, ...]} or {\"status\": \"infeasible\"}.\n\nTHIS CANDIDATE\n--------------\nPer-rule minimal-investment solvers (``min_investment_*``). Exact (up to the numerical margin):\n  * mean      closed form (L1: total gap * T, any allocation; L0: fewest tasks whose headroom covers it)\n  * median    odd T: cheapest tasks to push above the best rival's median; even T: enumerate the pair of\n              middle order statistics (exact for L1 with uniform caps and for L0)\n  * maximin   raise every task below the best rival's minimum\n  * plurality choose which tasks to win; rivals lose a win when the target overtakes their unique lead, so\n              per task-count s the rival-specific quotas are met by cheapest-first picks (exact)\nHeuristic (near-optimal, always verified, then coordinate-pruned):\n  * trimmed   L1: \"floor\" plans (raise everything except the p lowest tasks to a common level, bisection);\n              the rate-1 phase of the trimmed mean is solved exactly by this family\n  * borda     L1: convex-hull (cost per rank passed) greedy over tasks; L0: greedy with restarts\n  * copeland  L1: ratio greedy over (task, level) moves; L0: greedy with restarts\n  * zscore    L1: floor family + steepest-ascent steps; L0: greedy with restarts\nEvery candidate plan (including the starter's baseline plan) is re-applied to X and re-scored with an\nexact replica of the rules (``verify_ranks_first``); the cheapest verified plan is returned. Any internal\nerror falls back to the original starter routine.\n\nCycle 3 addition: a time-budgeted polish (``_polish_plan``) on the cheapest verified plan: per-task bisection to\nthe verification boundary, dropping redundant boosted tasks, and pairwise transfer moves (L1: ladder of step\nsizes; L0: two-for-one swaps). Every accepted change is re-verified with ``verify_ranks_first``; the polished\nplan is returned only if verified and not costlier, otherwise the pre-polish plan is returned.\n\nThe module also holds offline analysis helpers (data manifest, bootstrap CI, Holm-corrected paired Wilcoxon\ntests, task subsampling, ablations, breadth-constrained cost curves). ``handle`` never calls them.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_MARGIN = 1e-7          # starter margin\n_SUCCESS = 2e-8         # margin demanded locally (evaluator needs > 1e-9)\n_ALREADY = 1e-8         # target already first if margin above this\n_TARGET_EPS = 1.5e-7    # aggregate-scale margin aimed at by closed forms\n_TIE_EPS = 1e-6         # per-task strict-win offset\n_BUDGET_S = 5.0         # solve-time budget (evaluator limit is 12 s per episode in total)\n_POLISH_BUDGET_S = 2.0  # wall-clock budget of the post-processing polish stage (per episode)\n_POLISH_MIN_LEFT_S = 1.0  # skip the polish if fewer than this many seconds of the solve budget remain\n_POLISH_PAD = 1e-9      # tiny pad above the bisected boundary (discrete rules flip at exact float ties)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
